   217	Same line. Same step. He had it before Karis said it, because he had counted it, and she said it anyway, to the ground and not to any of them: "Same stride. All of us." Then she walked forward, to the place, and not one step past it, and bent, and took up a stone from the road's edge the size of two fists, and set it in the rut at her heel, on the near side, where hers had come back, and Brom's, and Seln's, and, coming back from further in, Lira's. She straightened and looked at the stone. She did not write yet.
