    51	The five waded after. It was a hundred yards of gravel under a foot of quick water, cold enough to make the bones of his feet ache. The tape told him where the edge was whenever a stone turned under him. He kept his breath shallow and his eyes on the cart's tail. Three boxes sat on it under a sheet of patched canvas, left and middle and right, with the corner that was worn white turned outward. On top of them, roped down by her own instructions, sat Karis, who had been lifted up there like a sack and had made no objection.
    52	
    53	On the south bank he stopped to put his boots on, and saw the prints.
