   138	
   139	"The middle of the day."
   140	
   141	"You can see the middle of the day. It's up there."
   142	
   143	"I can see near enough. She didn't say near enough." He had his eyes on the rod's shadow, which lay along the grass to the north, as long as his hand and growing shorter. "She said a week from the middle of the eightieth. I was there. I saw where the rock's shadow lay when she took her hands off it."
   144	
   145	So they ate, and the shadow drew in. Nobody spoke of it, but Cael noticed that nobody strayed far either. The carter chewed, and looked from the rod to the big man and back, with the mild puzzlement of a person watching the customs of a foreign hold.

