Pike's traverse line and its pricing (ch24) · the Fallow slip and seal (ch24) · Pike's speech; "two hundred times"; "What's the line?" / "You'll know… It stops." (ch24) · Seln, "learned to write inside" (ch25) · the Part-1 log (ch25) · Ephram's letter (ch26) · Karis, "Their map has no roads…" (ch26) · Oryn, "You're a stop. I've added you." … "Don't make it a long stop." (ch26) · Vell's letter (ch27) · the five lines at the rise and "Same stride. All of us." (ch27) · the log at the stone (ch27) · Karis's perimeter lines and "A circle is a made shape." (ch28) · Seln on the stake, two lines (ch28) · "Skin."; "It costs nothing…"; "I've a knife and fifteen years…"; Oryn's two lines (ch29) · Cael, "It was dark before," … "It's dark now." (ch29) · "None I own…"; "They live in here…" (ch30) · the log at the far lip (ch30).

**Markers planned (three):** the map gives Lira's clock line from mid-sentence; the packet gives Pike's speech about Teague and Brom's council line each with a gap inside it. Each gets `[[TIER-B: … — coordinator to supply protected text]]` on its own line, and the scene is written round it.

## What stays withheld

Only the two private tests, seen by nobody, and the read reopened on the floor; no log line calls any of it deployment. Shadow untouched. The word the line will later be given does not occur. "Made" is said once, by Karis, and the narration says nothing of who or how. The stake's stamp is "the registry's". Oryn reads nobody inside. No hound is seen. No name is minted. "Nineteen" does not occur. No season, month or weekday.

## Changes made while drafting

- **The moss (ch23)** is two hundred yards of laid logs, not a mile: a hundred and forty soft logs chalked in the better part of an hour would not fit a mile.
- **The trials' order (ch29)** is Karis, Brom, Seln, Lira, Oryn, as listed above; the two private tests fall in the quarter of an hour AFTER Oryn's crossings, while the five are each turned inward and the mule is being hobbled, not during her third crossing (he keeps her count of twenty at the stone). He goes a cord north to Brom's first turf "to rule the rows fair".
- **Seln's small trial** puts him four yards to the SOUTH of the row, with the low noon sun behind him.
- **Brom's trial** gained a second act: he lifts the middle box over the stone and finds that it weighs the same.
- **The stake (ch28):** Seln does not infer a series from the number ("I do not know what the number counts"). Cael counts it as the third thing after the query and the posting, and has a line with no direction on it.
- **Karis's window** gives no figure for her own pace; it says only that her count from the turn to the stone is larger than his eighty and that two pacings differed by one.
- **Chapter 26:** the Oxhollow carter leaves Lira's left boot standing at the barn door, and she hangs it on Oryn's mule at the east gate (ch27). Oryn's sum at the long house door ends "by the ninety-ninth".
- **Chapter 27:** the bowman comes to the east gate; the mule grazes across the stone at dusk with two feet on either side.
- **Chapter 30:** the tenth cord ends at the middle of the floor and Karis checks it by pacing to the rim four ways. The rubbings: ten whole and the eleventh half done when Seln lifts his hand. Cael spends a quarter of an hour past his own limit and has it "entered against me". Seln's reading at the den: this morning's prints, eight or nine animals, all outward to the east.
- **The Teague marker** stands in the room scene before his window, as planned; the scene after it leans only on what the packet's own summary gives (read twice, put back).
- **The Fallow slip, Pike's traverse line, both letters and the three protected log entries** are printed once each; later references are narration (two partial re-quotations of the slip in chapters 24, 25 and 30 were recomposed after the first draft).
- **Titles:** 23 "Round by the Ferry", 24 "Under the Stone", 25 "Tenth", 26 "White Paper", 27 "The Rise", 28 "Sixty-Two Cords", 29 "A Stride Inside", 30 "The Far Lip".

