+
+## Verdict
+
+**Four genuine tracked passages.** Chapter 30 scene 2 is densely tracked, with two passages in one scene. Chapter 29 scene 3 and chapter 30 scene 4 each contain one isolated passage; every other scene contains none.
+
+| Manuscript chapter | Scene 1 | Scene 2 | Scene 3 | Scene 4 | Scene 5 | Chapter total |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| 23 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **0** |
+| 24 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **0** |
+| 25 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **0** |
+| 26 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **0** |
+| 27 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **0** |
+| 28 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **0** |
+| 29 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 0 | 0 | **1** |
+| 30 | 0 | 2 | 0 | 1 | 0 | **3** |
+| **Movement total** |  |  |  |  |  | **4** |
+
+Scene numbers follow the manuscript's `---` divisions and the sweep probe. Line ranges are: chapter 23, 1–44 / 46–106 / 108–162 / 164–220 / 222–265; chapter 24, 1–58 / 60–116 / 118–176 / 178–224 / 226–275; chapter 25, 1–50 / 52–106 / 108–154 / 156–218 / 220–253; chapter 26, 1–40 / 42–106 / 108–152 / 154–216 / 218–261; chapter 27, 1–40 / 42–102 / 104–154 / 156–230 / 232–265; chapter 28, 1–62 / 64–104 / 106–144 / 146–188 / 190–239; chapter 29, 1–50 / 52–116 / 118–178 / 180–236 / 238–299; chapter 30, 1–30 / 32–100 / 102–152 / 154–216 / 218–239.
+
+## Tracked passages
+
+| chapter:line | Manuscript opening words | Source sentence followed | Kind | Beat chain to break without opening the source |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 29:131 | “He had watched her do that a thousand times…” | `books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-10.md:85` — “Cael watched the air. There was nothing to watch…” | varied | The required result is that Lira's full burst becomes one step. Beyond that, both tellings have Cael recognize the familiar preparation through an ordered list of body mechanics, watch her commit the whole body and release, and find that the complete effort has produced only an ordinary step and its small physical aftermath. Break the chain by entering after the step has landed, or make Lira report what she attempted before Cael reconstructs any part of the setup. |
+| 30:33 | “The edge was the first thing that he catalogued…” | `books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-10.md:193` — “The floor. He walked it edge to edge…” | near-verbatim | Both descriptions begin at the floor's edge, carry the rim all the way around, raise it a hand above the surrounding ground, and compare its smooth turnover to the rim of a shallow dish or basin before naming it a lip. The plan requires a lip, not this image and clause order. Enter on temperature or silence underfoot; discover the raised rim later when somebody crosses it or lays the cord over it, and use no vessel comparison. |
+| 30:57 | “She had the lid off the middle box.” | `books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-10.md:195` — “Karis had the middle box open on the floor by then…” | split | Karis opens the middle box, brings its masonry samples out one at a time, places each against the grey floor, looks from sample to floor, returns it, and only after the repeated comparisons announces that none matches. The nonmatch is required; this particular **open box → serial compare/look → replace → conclude none** procedure is not. Begin with one already failed comparison, group the samples by a visible property, or let another character notice that Karis has silently exhausted the box before she states the result. |
+| 30:155 | “Seln did not come back round.” | `books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-10.md:213` — “He had walked round the floor's edge on the outside of the lip…” | split | Seln circles the outer lip, stops at the far side without calling, and Cael notices the stop and brings the others across to him before the den is revealed. The den and its signs are required, but this **silent stop → Cael notices → party converges → reveal** entrance repeats the source staging. Have Seln call them, let the hollow become visible while they pack the rubbings, or let Cael encounter the first print before realizing Seln is already at the mouth. |
+
+## Dense-scene rerouting
+
+### Chapter 30, scene 2 (lines 32–100)
+
+Use the bands as the entry point: Lira notices the cut marks from the turf before anyone steps onto the floor. Let that observation pull the group across the rim, then establish temperature and silence, run the diameter and level checks, and postpone the lip's shape until the cord or a boot catches on it. For the material test, enter after Karis has already rejected several samples; sort the remaining chips into two or three visible families and test only their representatives before she concludes that none matches. That order preserves the required floor, measurements, lip, samples, and bands without repeating either source sentence's discovery sequence.
+
+The chapter 29 and chapter 30 scene-4 findings can be repaired locally from the table and do not require wholesale scene restructuring.

